Replaced the uint16 index plus per-call null check/pointer arithmetic with a direct table of `MESG*` pointers, so the hot path is a single table load. Initialization still mirrors the original reverse-order overwrite behavior for identical results.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* table[65536] = { 0 };
    static bool init = false;

    if (!init)
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        init = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```